{"seq":17,"trial_id":"shared-brain-access-2026-11/hermes-opus-gbrain-open-mu-v031-dev/sy-01-quarrendon-ticket-numbers/r3","wall_ts":"2026-11-22T19:10:35.062Z","sim_ts":"2026-10-14T09:10:00-05:00","args_digest":"d78e84d899aa650622e75097b31c9e8463ca407fecb574d09dcfe9e9b7b6a255","actor":"assistant","via":"mcp","tool":"chat.postMessage","kind":"write","args":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","text":"Hi Dana. Moss has five notes in the shared files, and four of them are North digests. Only two of those mention Quarrendon Freight Lines ticket numbers:\n\n1. #4419: Thea Ramaswell reported gatehouse barcode scanners failing to read trailer tags at Door 14 on third shift. It was escalated to tier-2 for scanner firmware testing. Source: \"Moss: North cheat sheet (undated)\" (teams/team-north/digests/north-account-cheatsheet.md).\n2. #PD-4492: Thea submitted it on 4 Oct 2025. Eau Claire gatehouse kiosk drivers at Dock Doors 14-18 weren't getting SMS bay assignments. Support patched it the same evening, and Thea confirmed it was cleared on 5 Oct. There's also an action item to archive the kiosk logs before the 14 Oct 2025 maintenance window. Source: \"Moss: Sunday prep for Ruth\" (teams/team-north/digests/2025-10-05-north-sunday.md).\n\nMoss's other two notes that mention QFL have no ticket numbers: the 9/14/2025 North pipeline digest and the 3/23/2026 renewal check-in.\n\nThere's one more ticket outside Moss's notes: the QFL account page (last updated 2026-09-30) lists #4912, which is open with support for lag on the Gate_Dwell_Daily report at Bay 14 check-ins in the Superior yard. Also, Marcus's note on \"Quarendon Freightways\" is about a different company, a non-customer, so I left it out."},"outcome":"ok","effect":{"channel":"DSHARED0001","ts":"1791987000.000124"}}
